  "EditorMetadata": {
    "Description": "P1b proof (GAP-1, Hill-attack -> Blueprints slice 4): Condition_AreAllAtBaseline rebuilt as a visually-authored AiPrimitive BTreeCondition, exercising the NEW in-body Branch -> inline if/else scheduler path together with P2 (foreign-entity component read) and P1a (FlowForEach loop). Graph: init WorkingState bool AllAtBaseline=true (Literal->SetVariable), then FlowForEach over the commander's UnitRoster (curated UnitRosterOps.Count/Subordinate) whose body reads each subordinate's NavigationStatus.Result via GetComponent(Target=CurrentItem) and, through the GAP-12 stopgap helper HillAssault2NavOps.IsArrived, BRANCHES: on 'not arrived' (Branch.False) it sets AllAtBaseline=false; on 'arrived' (Branch.True, unwired) nothing -- i.e. the AND-reduce `if (!IsArrived(nav.Result)) AllAtBaseline=false;` emitted as a nested inline if/else INSIDE the for-loop (P1b), not a BFS block split. After the loop, GetVariable(AllAtBaseline)->Branch returns Success/Failure. Proves in-body branch lowering (IrOp_If) end-to-end through the real netstandard2.0 generator. GAP-12: the enum-equality check still lives in the tiny pure IsArrived helper until a native Compare node lands, at which point this becomes fully visual. Does not modify the C# oracle (HillAttackCommanderNodes.Condition_AreAllAtBaseline).",
    "Category": null,
    "Recipe": null
